      "problem": "Solve for $j$ where $\\frac{j-4}{5}=\\frac{8+j}{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{j-4}{5} & =\\frac{8+j}{4} \\\\ (j-4)\\cdot 4 & =5\\cdot (8+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(j-4)\\cdot 4 & =5\\cdot (8+j) \\\\ 4j-16 & =40+5j \\\\ 4j-16-4j & =40+5j-4j \\\\ -16 & =40+j \\\\ -16-40 & =40+j-40 \\\\ -56 & =j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $j=-56.$",
